From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Dec 2020 22:05:18 +0000
Subject: spelling

We want the past tense of "stop", i.e., "stopped", while "stoped"
would be the English past tense of the German loan-word "stope",
meaning a single excavation in a mine.
